      "updated": 1784614932686,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To merge this sorted linked \nlist , we have these two solutions\n\n1. Take a array and put all the \nvalues of linked list in that , \nsuch that we can sort the \narray , and then convert it to \nthe linked list\n\n2.brute force way is done \n\n3. to solve this problem \noptimally , we have to solve this \nwithout an array \n\n: To make a dummy node with \nnew ListNode(-1) , then compare\nvalue , then move forward \nthe node",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To merge this sorted linked \nlist , we have these two solutions\n\n1. Take a array and put all the \nvalues of linked list in that , \nsuch that we can sort the \narray , and then convert it to \nthe linked list\n\n2.brute force way is done \n\n3. to solve this problem \noptimally , we have to solve this \nwithout an array \n\n: To make a dummy node with \nnew ListNode(-1) , then compare\nvalue , then move forward \nthe node",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
